<title>FRANCE: NordLB plans to set 2.0 bln Ffr bond by end 1996.</title>
<headline>NordLB plans to set 2.0 bln Ffr bond by end 1996.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norddeutsche Landesbank Girozentrale board member Jurgen Kosters said on Tuesday it plans to issue a two billion French franc bond by the end of 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;We are going to issue two billion francs with a maturity between six and 10 years, depending on market conditions,&quot; he told the news conference in Paris.</p>
<p>Kosters said the bank was aiming for a spread over French government bonds of between 15 and 17 basis points.</p>
<p>Caisse des Depots et Consignations has been awarded the mandate for the bond issue.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
